WEBVTT

00:04.130 --> 00:07.540
Do you think those people yesterday were part of the same group?

00:07.540 --> 00:11.910
Perhaps. Their timing was a little too good.

00:11.910 --> 00:15.430
Eins, Zwei, Drei, Vier...

00:16.380 --> 00:20.040
are German for one, two, three, and four.

00:23.050 --> 00:23.880
So you're saying...

00:24.650 --> 00:27.490
those guys were part of a single team.

00:32.160 --> 00:37.470
Hey who are you thinking of now?

00:37.470 --> 00:45.370
I am thinking of you

00:48.010 --> 00:50.680
I felt it when I opened my window

00:50.680 --> 00:52.910
Ah the smell of the night

00:52.910 --> 00:55.520
Whose face did I just see

00:55.520 --> 00:57.790
In my heart?

00:57.790 --> 01:00.560
When I was

01:00.560 --> 01:02.820
Soaked by the cold rain

01:02.820 --> 01:04.460
You were the only one

01:04.460 --> 01:07.430
To reach out your hand

01:07.430 --> 01:12.270
Why are you always

01:12.270 --> 01:16.910
The one to support me

01:16.910 --> 01:19.840
Each time

01:19.840 --> 01:24.110
I fall deeper in love

01:24.110 --> 01:29.350
Hey no matter what I do I want to see you

01:29.350 --> 01:34.060
Falling in love hurts

01:34.060 --> 01:36.790
You are always the only reason

01:36.790 --> 01:39.360
I feel happiness and heartache

01:39.360 --> 01:47.230
I am thinking of you

01:50.140 --> 01:58.740
Hey I want to see you

02:03.050 --> 02:06.050
The

02:03.050 --> 02:06.050
Holy

02:03.050 --> 02:06.050
Woman's

02:03.050 --> 02:06.050
Advent

02:03.380 --> 02:07.780
I believe my headache is related to the seal barrier.

02:08.920 --> 02:09.960
In other words,

02:09.960 --> 02:12.930
the presence of those attempting to break

02:12.930 --> 02:15.450
through the barrier causes your head to hurt?

02:16.100 --> 02:17.300
Yes.

02:17.300 --> 02:20.970
That's why I want to learn more about the seal.

02:20.970 --> 02:22.040
I get it.

02:22.040 --> 02:24.010
But you stay at home.

02:24.010 --> 02:25.800
What? Why?

02:28.280 --> 02:31.650
Those guys will come for the Artifacts again.

02:31.650 --> 02:33.780
If we run into them, it'll be a real pain.

02:33.780 --> 02:36.250
Even though they're my headaches?

02:36.250 --> 02:38.690
How about we ask Ohmi?

02:40.690 --> 02:42.460
Ask him what?

02:42.460 --> 02:44.980
The seal is created by the Artifacts.

02:45.330 --> 02:49.090
And the one who knows the most about the Artifacts is Ohmi.

02:49.500 --> 02:51.730
Lady Baba trusts him.

02:51.730 --> 02:54.640
He's the Shugogo house's mediator, too.

02:54.640 --> 02:56.100
Is that right?

02:57.170 --> 02:58.110
Someone's here.

03:02.340 --> 03:05.970
What are you guys doing here?

03:08.220 --> 03:10.750
Uh, um...

03:10.750 --> 03:11.950
Sorry!

03:15.360 --> 03:17.350
I'm joking. Joking.

03:18.760 --> 03:19.780
Huh?

03:20.760 --> 03:22.160
What about you?

03:22.160 --> 03:23.330
What are you doing here?

03:23.330 --> 03:28.000
There aren't any school regulations that say I can't be here.

03:29.670 --> 03:34.210
Miss, were you listening to our conversation?

03:34.210 --> 03:35.840
What? Why?

03:35.840 --> 03:38.810
Were you talking about something I shouldn't hear?

03:39.410 --> 03:41.380
No, absolutely not!

03:43.890 --> 03:45.620
It's already time for class.

03:45.620 --> 03:47.050
That's too bad.

03:49.490 --> 03:50.460
Let's go.

03:53.760 --> 03:54.890
Here I go!

03:57.270 --> 03:59.260
Did something happen yesterday?

04:00.740 --> 04:04.040
When you were leaving you looked pale,

04:04.040 --> 04:06.440
and you were talking with Onizaki.

04:07.940 --> 04:11.280
If something's bothering you, you can always talk to me.

04:12.380 --> 04:15.010
Especially if it's a love problem, leave it to me!

04:17.090 --> 04:18.880
That's not it.

04:19.420 --> 04:21.290
But thank you, really.

04:21.290 --> 04:22.920
It makes me happy.

04:23.760 --> 04:26.230
What? Don't be so formal.

04:26.230 --> 04:29.100
We're friends so of course I'd worry.

04:34.140 --> 04:35.260
He's late.

04:35.470 --> 04:37.710
Shinji is late.

04:37.710 --> 04:39.200
It's probably a girl again.

04:40.310 --> 04:43.010
Shinji is pretty cute.

04:43.110 --> 04:44.380
Hey!

04:44.380 --> 04:46.580
Don't call a guy cute!

04:46.580 --> 04:47.810
Remember that!

04:48.650 --> 04:50.550
Okay. Sorry.

04:51.420 --> 04:53.190
Sorry to keep you!

04:53.190 --> 04:54.660
What were you doing?

04:54.660 --> 04:56.890
He was keeping some girls company.

04:57.930 --> 04:58.990
Let's go.

04:58.990 --> 05:00.330
Ohmi is waiting.

05:00.660 --> 05:03.100
Th-Th-That's not true!

05:03.670 --> 05:06.130
Let's go, Yuichi.

05:11.770 --> 05:13.040
But seriously!

05:13.470 --> 05:15.280
Upperclassman, you didn't see it.

05:13.910 --> 05:15.140
Itou Super

05:15.280 --> 05:16.110
Why not?!

05:16.110 --> 05:17.740
Thank you very much.

05:19.150 --> 05:20.620
Mitsuru!

05:20.620 --> 05:22.350
You're all here together.

05:22.350 --> 05:23.850
What are you doing here?

05:23.850 --> 05:25.720
I'm getting groceries for dinner.

05:25.720 --> 05:27.120
Where's the meat?

05:27.290 --> 05:31.060
Tonight will be fried Japanese blue fish and boiled potatoes.

05:31.690 --> 05:35.600
Sorry, Mitsuru.
I might be a little late tonight.

05:35.860 --> 05:37.660
I'm visiting Suguru's house.

05:38.130 --> 05:40.570
That's all right. We'll wait.

05:41.370 --> 05:44.140
Could this have something to do with the fight last night?

05:44.140 --> 05:47.770
Yes. You could say we figured something out.

05:48.180 --> 05:50.080
I thought I would ask him.

05:50.610 --> 05:51.940
I understand.

05:53.510 --> 05:54.980
You're going, too?

06:00.320 --> 06:03.720
I've heard you haven't realized your powers yet.

06:04.190 --> 06:08.150
What do you plan to do in that mediocre state?

06:09.100 --> 06:12.730
But I'm a member of the
Shugogo house as well.

06:12.730 --> 06:14.670
I have to fulfill my duties.

06:14.870 --> 06:17.040
Sending half a man to fight.

06:17.040 --> 06:18.770
I cannot agree with it.

06:19.340 --> 06:20.360
Excuse me.

06:24.410 --> 06:26.940
She's tough on you, like always.

06:27.720 --> 06:29.210
Like always?

06:29.350 --> 06:30.520
When we were kids,

06:30.520 --> 06:33.490
he would always get scolded by Mitsuru.

06:33.490 --> 06:35.480
She used to make him cry.

06:35.990 --> 06:38.790
Please stop with those old stories.

06:39.330 --> 06:40.430
I see.

06:40.430 --> 06:43.160
So that's why Mitsuru was so mad.

06:43.160 --> 06:44.700
She was worried about him.

06:44.700 --> 06:46.330
Even you, Tamaki?

06:47.140 --> 06:49.930
She's known you all for so long.

06:50.570 --> 06:54.240
I want to know more about the seal, but about all of you as well.

06:55.740 --> 06:57.510
What's your favorite hobby.

06:58.650 --> 07:02.980
Is this somehow related to keeping you safe?

07:03.250 --> 07:05.120
It is! Very much so!

07:05.590 --> 07:09.750
It isn't a bad thing to know each person's idiosyncrasies.

07:10.560 --> 07:12.580
So, Shinji, what about you?

07:13.430 --> 07:18.530
Cooking. Stuffed cabbage, or a fluffy omelet over rice.

07:19.370 --> 07:20.800
That sounds delicious!

07:21.240 --> 07:22.460
That's nice.

07:22.840 --> 07:25.400
You're really trying to get him to cook for you, aren't you?

07:25.910 --> 07:27.640
Leave me alone.

07:27.880 --> 07:30.870
What about you, Mahiro?
What's your hobby?

07:31.010 --> 07:32.480
For me, bikes.

07:33.450 --> 07:34.820
You ride a bike?

07:34.820 --> 07:36.580
Yeah, I plan to.

07:36.980 --> 07:39.890
In exchange for staying in this town,

07:39.890 --> 07:42.410
they've promised to buy me one.

07:43.930 --> 07:46.550
You're not buying one, but having one bought for you?

07:46.760 --> 07:47.920
Good luck.

07:48.830 --> 07:51.530
What? Are you guys making fun of me?

07:51.530 --> 07:54.530
Stop it. This is just hypothetical.

07:55.270 --> 07:56.790
What about you, Takuma?

07:57.440 --> 07:58.940
Me?

07:58.940 --> 08:01.140
I guess crossword puzzles.

08:03.480 --> 08:05.240
And Yuichi?

08:07.110 --> 08:10.780
I like lying in the sun and just relaxing.

08:10.950 --> 08:12.120
That's it?

08:12.120 --> 08:13.110
That's it.

08:13.350 --> 08:15.080
You sound like an old man.

08:16.020 --> 08:19.130
But now that I said it, that's very you.

08:19.130 --> 08:20.530
Is that so?

08:20.530 --> 08:21.660
And you?

08:21.660 --> 08:23.820
Everyone said theirs, what's yours?

08:24.470 --> 08:25.800
Me?

08:25.800 --> 08:27.830
How do I put it...

08:28.000 --> 08:30.440
What is it? Just say it.

08:34.840 --> 08:37.240
Visiting shrines and temples.

08:38.410 --> 08:40.580
Y-You're such an old lady!

08:40.580 --> 08:42.680
You really can't talk.

08:43.180 --> 08:47.280
Shut up! I like what I like, so what can I do?!

08:49.890 --> 08:52.520
Banzai! Japanese traditional culture!

08:53.230 --> 08:55.200
Suguru...

08:56.400 --> 09:00.030
I heard you talking.

09:00.030 --> 09:02.400
See? This is what happens when you're loud.

09:02.400 --> 09:05.340
Mahiro, you were laughing the most.

09:05.910 --> 09:08.240
Why don't you have some tea?

09:08.240 --> 09:11.010
I even have Onizaki's favorite taiyaki.

09:11.780 --> 09:14.550
What? Takuma, you like taiyaki?

09:14.550 --> 09:15.980
Who cares, right?

09:16.850 --> 09:19.510
Tamaki, what tea would you like?

09:20.390 --> 09:21.520
Um...

09:27.260 --> 09:30.600
Are these all different teas?

09:30.600 --> 09:33.070
Yes. What about green tea?

09:34.100 --> 09:35.230
I'd love it!

09:39.640 --> 09:40.900
It's so good!

09:41.510 --> 09:44.600
Suguru, are you a tea master?

09:45.810 --> 09:46.950
Close!

09:46.950 --> 09:49.010
Ohmi is a calligraphy teacher.

09:49.680 --> 09:52.220
From black tea to green tea,

09:52.220 --> 09:54.420
my hobby is collecting teas.

09:54.990 --> 09:59.620
I tried a few, but each one was delicious.

10:00.160 --> 10:02.930
It makes me happy to hear you say that.

10:05.830 --> 10:09.430
Now, you wanted to know more about the Artifacts, right?

10:10.300 --> 10:11.570
Y-Yes.

10:16.240 --> 10:19.370
Firstly, why we call it an Artifact?

10:20.150 --> 10:23.680
This is because it originally belonged to Tamayori princess

10:23.680 --> 10:25.880
and was passed down through the generations.

10:26.690 --> 10:28.360
Is that so?

10:28.360 --> 10:30.880
Why the "Is that so?"

10:32.290 --> 10:36.730
I thought the Tamayori princess was a person from the distant past.

10:37.200 --> 10:42.870
Knowing that something of hers still remains makes her seem so much closer.

10:43.200 --> 10:44.840
So that's why.

10:44.840 --> 10:46.170
I'm sorry.

10:46.170 --> 10:47.470
Please continue.

10:48.780 --> 10:51.580
The Artifact consists of the Magatani necklace,

10:52.310 --> 10:53.300
the bracelet,

10:54.850 --> 10:55.820
the bells,

10:57.420 --> 10:58.390
the mirror,

11:01.490 --> 11:04.290
and the ring, which makes five.

11:04.290 --> 11:06.780
They're all decorative.

11:07.800 --> 11:10.960
So, Mahiro, you didn't know either.

11:12.530 --> 11:13.930
I don't have to!

11:14.540 --> 11:20.040
The five Artifacts are responsible for sealing the Onikirimaru,

11:20.040 --> 11:23.840
but there is no difference in strength.

11:24.610 --> 11:26.050
In addition to sealing,

11:26.050 --> 11:29.680
it also is a barrier that keeps out intruders,

11:29.680 --> 11:34.360
so only the one with the
Tamayori princess's blood

11:34.360 --> 11:37.550
and the Shugogo house can enter.

11:43.060 --> 11:46.130
Did he return to his group?

11:46.570 --> 11:50.160
Answer, Magus, the user of magic.

11:51.510 --> 11:55.180
Indeed. The seal has weakened.

11:55.180 --> 11:58.170
The time has finally come,

11:58.850 --> 12:01.340
the holy Monado.

12:04.350 --> 12:06.910
Then let's get started.

12:09.920 --> 12:14.730
The seal has weakened before,

12:14.730 --> 12:17.430
but now that the enemy has shown itself...

12:17.430 --> 12:20.270
I don't intend on letting them put a finger on it.

12:20.270 --> 12:21.760
Obviously!

12:24.440 --> 12:27.170
O-chan, if you're willing to say that, then I'm not worried.

12:28.540 --> 12:31.670
Looks like she believes in us less than the Osaki fox.

12:32.880 --> 12:35.540
Of course I believe in you.

12:36.450 --> 12:38.520
You just ate, didn't you?

12:38.520 --> 12:39.990
Leave me alone.

12:40.720 --> 12:42.660
It's that late already?

12:43.320 --> 12:45.230
Kotokura is probably waiting.

12:47.190 --> 12:48.730
Suguru.

12:48.730 --> 12:51.560
Thank you very much, and thank you for the food.

12:52.000 --> 12:54.700
No. I don't know if I was much use.

12:55.540 --> 12:57.060
Thank you for having us.

12:58.110 --> 12:59.240
Come back anytime.

12:59.240 --> 13:00.440
Goodbye.

12:59.970 --> 13:01.210
By the way...

13:01.210 --> 13:03.310
May I ask one thing, Ohmi?

13:03.310 --> 13:05.110
Four characters that start with "hi,"

13:05.110 --> 13:06.850
Hizakozou Muragawa.

13:05.450 --> 13:06.850
So it's true...

13:07.110 --> 13:16.580
Crossword

13:07.620 --> 13:10.020
Why would I lie?

13:10.790 --> 13:14.190
You used to ask me when you didn't know before, too.

13:14.760 --> 13:16.420
You were cute back then.

13:16.860 --> 13:18.660
Is that right?

13:18.660 --> 13:22.620
Suguru, you knew Takuma when he was young?

13:23.330 --> 13:24.600
Yes.

13:24.600 --> 13:27.900
Inukai was away for a while,

13:27.900 --> 13:30.300
but everyone was born and raised here.

13:30.300 --> 13:32.740
I've known them all since they were kids.

13:34.140 --> 13:37.110
Let's not talk about the past, Ohmi.

13:38.310 --> 13:40.080
The answer is "Hikagami."

13:40.080 --> 13:42.620
Hikagami... Thank you very much.

13:42.620 --> 13:43.380
Now I can solve it!

13:43.380 --> 13:49.060
You know, no one's seen you solve a puzzle by yourself.

13:49.060 --> 13:50.790
What is that supposed to mean?

13:51.530 --> 13:52.520
So-

13:56.460 --> 13:57.860
Hey, what happened?

13:59.800 --> 14:01.060
They're back?

14:03.370 --> 14:04.630
They're back?

14:11.450 --> 14:13.780
But, Tamaki, what will you...

14:15.250 --> 14:16.810
What are you doing?

14:19.190 --> 14:20.680
I'm going with you.

14:22.020 --> 14:22.990
But...

14:22.990 --> 14:27.330
You didn't think the Tamayori princess would go somewhere

14:27.330 --> 14:29.400
without the Shugogo protectors, did you?

14:29.400 --> 14:32.500
It's safer if everyone stays together.

14:32.500 --> 14:36.030
You can just sit real pretty.

14:41.710 --> 14:44.340
I thought it was here...

14:45.510 --> 14:47.280
If I'm wrong, sorry.

14:48.550 --> 14:50.250
No, they'll come.

14:50.250 --> 14:52.550
They provoked us.

15:16.210 --> 15:17.080
Worthless.

15:18.280 --> 15:20.450
Who are you?

15:20.450 --> 15:23.820
Who? Oh, you're talking to me.

15:26.350 --> 15:29.850
I suppose there's a need to introduce myself.

15:36.430 --> 15:38.230
The long haired one is Eins.

15:39.430 --> 15:41.400
The man with the sickle is Zwei.

15:42.100 --> 15:45.670
The old man with the cane is Drei, the Magus.

15:45.670 --> 15:47.640
Sorry about yesterday.

15:47.640 --> 15:49.910
Let's get along in the future.

15:49.910 --> 15:53.610
The one on top of the tree branch is Vier.

15:54.450 --> 15:56.450
And I am

15:56.450 --> 15:59.820
the incarnation of Monado Cephelot,

15:59.820 --> 16:03.590
All of Logos, Aria Rosenberg.

16:03.890 --> 16:08.850
I've come to take something of mine.

16:11.330 --> 16:13.600
You're kidding.

16:13.600 --> 16:16.300
I don't have time to play with kids!

16:19.140 --> 16:20.470
Eins, Zwei.

16:32.950 --> 16:34.720
This guy...

16:36.160 --> 16:38.250
That stung a little!

16:44.030 --> 16:45.020
Accelerate.

16:48.840 --> 16:49.770
Strengthen.

17:17.000 --> 17:19.060
Shisui Fuzehi Bonsui!

17:27.010 --> 17:28.130
Vanish

17:34.520 --> 17:37.850
It's pretty easy when your opponent uses brute force.

17:37.850 --> 17:39.340
Kyoshu Gorai Shinsh-

17:41.620 --> 17:42.890
An illusion?

17:43.690 --> 17:45.020
Let me return the favor!

18:08.780 --> 18:10.150
So strong...

18:11.720 --> 18:13.490
Don't you get it?

18:13.490 --> 18:16.320
They're just testing them.

18:18.660 --> 18:19.850
Show them.

18:37.580 --> 18:40.780
Don't worry. It's over now.

18:41.120 --> 18:44.450
Losing something important to you is painful.

19:17.820 --> 19:19.380
Let's go.

19:23.120 --> 19:24.590
I won't let you!

19:28.300 --> 19:29.320
Stop!

19:41.810 --> 19:42.970
Shit.

19:49.780 --> 19:52.750
It's me. How are things over there?

19:54.190 --> 19:56.760
Nice. Good job getting it.

19:56.760 --> 19:59.190
They've started to move over here.

20:00.890 --> 20:04.330
Right, the Logos.

20:04.330 --> 20:08.000
Also, surprisingly, Monado is leading it.

20:10.000 --> 20:12.210
That's right. That holy woman.

20:12.210 --> 20:14.200
I saw her in the flesh for the first time.

20:17.240 --> 20:22.910
I've heard there's too much of a strength difference with the Tamayori side.

20:27.220 --> 20:29.320
What is our next move going to be?

20:30.860 --> 20:32.720
Understood. Until later.

20:41.200 --> 20:42.930
How elegant.

20:50.340 --> 20:52.450
She'll be right here.

20:52.450 --> 20:53.710
One moment.

20:55.250 --> 20:56.220
Yes.

21:01.790 --> 21:04.660
Are you sure you don't want to go to the hospital?

21:05.230 --> 21:06.890
If I rest for a night I'll be fine.

21:06.890 --> 21:08.160
A night?

21:08.930 --> 21:12.890
We told you, we have different blood in our veins.

21:13.530 --> 21:16.500
This is nothing more than a scratch.

21:17.070 --> 21:18.410
But...

21:18.410 --> 21:21.170
It's all right. You don't need to worry.

21:27.580 --> 21:29.880
I believe Lady Baba is here.

21:41.300 --> 21:45.300
From between the trees

21:45.300 --> 21:53.210
The evening sun spills onto this tree lined street

21:53.210 --> 21:58.710
Talking and laughing

21:58.710 --> 22:04.120
Mysteriously made me feel at ease

22:06.620 --> 22:12.960
Since the two of us met that day

22:12.960 --> 22:16.830
Through the time we have spent together

22:16.830 --> 22:26.830
This feeling has grown

22:30.310 --> 22:33.010
In order to protect you

22:33.010 --> 22:38.620
I am here right now

22:38.620 --> 22:44.490
You try to act strong

22:44.490 --> 22:49.230
But I will accept all your weaknesses

22:49.230 --> 22:52.070
No matter how small

22:52.070 --> 22:57.500
You can rely on me for anything

22:57.500 --> 23:04.810
If you trip I will catch you with these hands

23:13.750 --> 23:14.810
Logos...

23:16.020 --> 23:17.590
That's what she called herself?

23:17.590 --> 23:18.720
Grandma...

23:18.890 --> 23:23.020
It is impossible for you to restore the Artifact's seal.

23:25.370 --> 23:30.360
This is because you have not realized yourself as the Tamayori princess.

23:36.310 --> 23:37.680
Did you enjoy it?

23:38.680 --> 23:42.010
I had a lot of fun.

23:46.650 --> 23:49.620
If you come back again, I'd be happy.

23:50.790 --> 23:53.660
I'll be waiting here.

23:55.230 --> 24:00.960
Next Time: The Two Tasks
